==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|lighty}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|lyghtly}}, {{m|enm|liȝtliche}}, {{m|enm|lihtliche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lēohtlīċe}}, equivalent to {{af|en|light|-ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlaɪtli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-lightly.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪtli|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[light]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|As a teacher, I don't take rudeness in class '''lightly'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|VIII|passage=Elbows almost touching they leaned at ease, idly reading the almost obliterated lines engraved there. &para; {{nowrap|"I never}} understood it," she observed, '''lightly''' scornful. "What occult meaning has a sun-dial for the spooney? ''I'm'' sure I don't want to read riddles in a strange gentleman's optics."}}

